{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2566 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "2b685ec1e2f8ef086991cb283c8b6e7b07277110f61fabf6bd4106300c633ddc" :edb/db-before-t 2565 :edb/db-after-t 2566 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535878 50 #inst "2026-10-15T03:37:49.301Z" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186096619 1038 #edb/ref 17592186536061 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186096619 1038 #edb/ref 17592186536065 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186096619 1038 #edb/ref 17592186536069 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186096619 1038 #edb/ref 17592186536071 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186096619 1038 #edb/ref 17592186536074 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186096619 1038 #edb/ref 17592186536075 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186096619 1038 #edb/ref 17592186536077 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186096619 1038 #edb/ref 17592186536087 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186096619 1038 #edb/ref 17592186536090 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186096619 1038 #edb/ref 17592186536098 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186096619 1040 #edb/ref 17592186536099 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536061 1068 #edb/ref 17592186536066 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536061 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536061 1071 "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=(3 x^{2} + x - 1)\\cdot (\\ln{\\left(x \\right)})$, calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=e^{2}$.\n\nSlope $=$ {{field-1}}" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536061 1072 #uuid "025970ae-87f8-5c12-8836-70b62439e2c5" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536061 1074 "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=3 x^{2} + x - 1$ and $v(x)=\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\nu'(x)=6 x + 1,\\quad v'(x)=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx} &=uv'(x)+vu'(x) \\\\ &=(3 x^{2} + x - 1)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x})+(\\ln{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (6 x + 1) \\\\ &=\\frac{6 x^{2} \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} + 3 x^{2} + x \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} + x - 1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=e^{2}$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left.\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx}\\right|_{x=e^{2}} &=(3 (e^{2})^{2} + (e^{2}) - 1)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{(e^{2})})+(\\ln{\\left((e^{2}) \\right)})\\cdot (6 (e^{2}) + 1) \\\\ &=(-1 + e^{2} + 3 e^{4})\\cdot (e^{-2})+(2)\\cdot (1 + 6 e^{2}) \\\\ &=- \\frac{1}{e^{2}} + 3 + 15 e^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $- \\frac{1}{e^{2}} + 3 + 15 e^{2}.$" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536062 1080 "-8" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536062 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536062 1083 #uuid "0abdf3e2-3942-5519-a3a0-98c8ba14955a" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536063 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2} \\left(9 \\pi^{2} + 112 + 60 \\pi\\right)}{32}" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536063 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536063 1083 #uuid "0e717ad5-c501-5b39-af7e-8878ba6ee6f9" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536064 1080 "5" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536064 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536064 1083 #uuid "0f87e3eb-6bcd-53ef-bb03-fc2a22a36834" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536065 1068 #edb/ref 17592186536079 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536065 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536065 1071 "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=(4 e^{x})\\cdot (x + 1)$, calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=0$." 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536065 1072 #uuid "11508a06-1238-59d6-9f30-ce054ca95db7" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536065 1074 "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=4 e^{x}$ and $v(x)=x + 1.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\nu'(x)=4 e^{x},\\quad v'(x)=1.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx} &=uv'(x)+vu'(x) \\\\ &=(4 e^{x})\\cdot (1)+(x + 1)\\cdot (4 e^{x}) \\\\ &=4 \\left(x + 2\\right) e^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=0$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left.\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx}\\right|_{x=0} &=(4 e^{(0)})\\cdot (1)+((0) + 1)\\cdot (4 e^{(0)}) \\\\ &=(4)\\cdot (1)+(1)\\cdot (4) \\\\ &=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $8.$" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536066 1075 #edb/ref 17592186536086 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536066 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536066 1077 "field-1" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536066 1078 #edb/ref 17592186536086 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536066 1079 #uuid "1461180d-25fe-52b1-abad-c2120615be94" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536067 1075 #edb/ref 17592186536063 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536067 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536067 1077 "field-1" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536067 1078 #edb/ref 17592186536063 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536067 1079 #uuid "1d6f8461-59dd-570a-8790-4ee15ed4552d" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536068 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2} \\left(- 12 \\pi - 32 - \\pi^{2}\\right)}{32}" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536068 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536068 1083 #uuid "27c49a10-bf3d-5b30-aa62-004fc1530f0b" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536069 1068 #edb/ref 17592186536092 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536069 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536069 1071 "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=(- x^{2} - x - 1)\\cdot (\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})$, calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.\n\nSlope $=$ {{field-1}}" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536069 1072 #uuid "33ab5b35-dd61-5afa-9e50-76ac2177002e" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536069 1074 "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=- x^{2} - x - 1$ and $v(x)=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\nu'(x)=- 2 x - 1,\\quad v'(x)=\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx} &=uv'(x)+vu'(x) \\\\ &=(- x^{2} - x - 1)\\cdot (\\cos{\\left(x \\right)})+(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (- 2 x - 1) \\\\ &=- x^{2} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} - 2 x \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - x \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left.\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx}\\right|_{x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}} &=(- (\\frac{\\pi}{4})^{2} - (\\frac{\\pi}{4}) - 1)\\cdot (\\cos{\\left((\\frac{\\pi}{4}) \\right)})+(\\sin{\\left((\\frac{\\pi}{4}) \\right)})\\cdot (- 2 (\\frac{\\pi}{4}) - 1) \\\\ &=(-1 - \\frac{\\pi}{4} - \\frac{\\pi^{2}}{16})\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})+(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})\\cdot (- \\frac{\\pi}{2} - 1) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{2} \\left(- 12 \\pi - 32 - \\pi^{2}\\right)}{32}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $\\frac{\\sqrt{2} \\left(- 12 \\pi - 32 - \\pi^{2}\\right)}{32}.$" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536070 1075 #edb/ref 17592186536091 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536070 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536070 1077 "field-1" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536070 1078 #edb/ref 17592186536091 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536070 1079 #uuid "354f12c4-c49c-5ce8-9d56-4a6bfbb09230" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536071 1068 #edb/ref 17592186536076 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536071 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536071 1071 "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=(- e^{x})\\cdot (x + 3)$, calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=0$." 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536071 1072 #uuid "3897814a-55c8-55e3-8f23-2d1a17edc389" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536071 1074 "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=- e^{x}$ and $v(x)=x + 3.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\nu'(x)=- e^{x},\\quad v'(x)=1.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx} &=uv'(x)+vu'(x) \\\\ &=(- e^{x})\\cdot (1)+(x + 3)\\cdot (- e^{x}) \\\\ &=- \\left(x + 4\\right) e^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=0$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left.\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx}\\right|_{x=0} &=(- e^{(0)})\\cdot (1)+((0) + 3)\\cdot (- e^{(0)}) \\\\ &=(-1)\\cdot (1)+(3)\\cdot (-1) \\\\ &=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $-4.$" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536072 1080 "9" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536072 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536072 1083 #uuid "396109d2-9a78-5ec7-8f4c-daf147bbb5a2" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536073 1080 "8" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536073 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536073 1083 #uuid "3bb39653-f774-5bc6-95ff-0532ba097430" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536074 1068 #edb/ref 17592186536083 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536074 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536074 1071 "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=(- 4 e^{x})\\cdot (x + 1)$, calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=0$.\n\nSlope $=$ {{field-1}}" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536074 1072 #uuid "3be093e9-a88a-5893-84f7-f2f4d4e8fb03" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536074 1074 "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=- 4 e^{x}$ and $v(x)=x + 1.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\nu'(x)=- 4 e^{x},\\quad v'(x)=1.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx} &=uv'(x)+vu'(x) \\\\ &=(- 4 e^{x})\\cdot (1)+(x + 1)\\cdot (- 4 e^{x}) \\\\ &=- 4 \\left(x + 2\\right) e^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=0$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left.\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx}\\right|_{x=0} &=(- 4 e^{(0)})\\cdot (1)+((0) + 1)\\cdot (- 4 e^{(0)}) \\\\ &=(-4)\\cdot (1)+(1)\\cdot (-4) \\\\ &=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $-8.$" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536075 1068 #edb/ref 17592186536082 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536075 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536075 1071 "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=(- x^{2} - 2 x + 2)\\cdot (\\ln{\\left(x \\right)})$, calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=e^{2}$.\n\nSlope $=$ {{field-1}}" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536075 1072 #uuid "3cc06495-0e47-5717-9700-118ad0cf690b" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536075 1074 "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=- x^{2} - 2 x + 2$ and $v(x)=\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\nu'(x)=- 2 x - 2,\\quad v'(x)=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx} &=uv'(x)+vu'(x) \\\\ &=(- x^{2} - 2 x + 2)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x})+(\\ln{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (- 2 x - 2) \\\\ &=- \\frac{2 x^{2} \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} + x^{2} + 2 x \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} + 2 x - 2}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=e^{2}$ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left.\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx}\\right|_{x=e^{2}} &=(- (e^{2})^{2} - 2 (e^{2}) + 2)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{(e^{2})})+(\\ln{\\left((e^{2}) \\right)})\\cdot (- 2 (e^{2}) - 2) \\\\ &=(- e^{4} - 2 e^{2} + 2)\\cdot (e^{-2})+(2)\\cdot (- 2 e^{2} - 2) \\\\ &=- 5 e^{2} - 6 + \\frac{2}{e^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $- 5 e^{2} - 6 + \\frac{2}{e^{2}}.$" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536076 1075 #edb/ref 17592186536084 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536076 1075 #edb/ref 17592186536088 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536076 1075 #edb/ref 17592186536093 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536076 1075 #edb/ref 17592186536094 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536076 1075 #edb/ref 17592186536097 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536076 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536076 1077 "selection" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536076 1078 #edb/ref 17592186536097 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536076 1079 #uuid "3ecdcf0c-044d-52db-b4c4-2ebdf6a193cc" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536077 1068 #edb/ref 17592186536070 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536077 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536077 1071 "If a curve $C$ is given by $y=(- 3 x^{2} + 3 x - 4)\\cdot (\\ln{\\left(x \\right)})$, calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=e$.\n\nSlope $=$ {{field-1}}" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536077 1072 #uuid "45e8eff6-7be8-5e2f-8927-eac30ddd0bc6" 13194139535878 17592186045443 true] [17592186536077 1074 "We differentiate using the product rule. Let $u(x)=- 3 x^{2} + 3 x - 4$ and $v(x)=\\ln{\\left(x 